From a0e55fdcc03e4140158ac17ab89b54cebe998f3e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 22:56:44 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Disc images read past 2 GiB on Windows; crash logger

- ga2_fileread (header-only): positional 64-bit reads (pread; ReadFile with a 64-bit OVERLAPPED offset). The Windows
  release's std::ifstream::seekg (llvm-mingw libc++) and long-based fseek stop at 2 GiB: the Mugen discs' SYSTEM.CNF
  lies at 4.2-4.5 GB, so the launcher found no BOOT2 line (issue #2; the 0.11.0 Windows launcher reproduces it under
  Wine, the Linux build was fine). Used by the launcher's ISO reader (native/launcher), the disc mount's overlays and
  segments taken from the image (the English pack's STRM.DAT segments), battlevr's disc reads; ps2_vfs host files
  seek with _fseeki64 / fseeko.
- Crash logger: a hard crash (SIGSEGV/SIGBUS/SIGILL/SIGFPE/SIGABRT; a Windows unhandled exception) writes its cause,
  the game time and (glibc) a backtrace to the log before it proceeds (issue #1's Steam Deck log ended with no word).

Verified: Mugen 1 imports with the fixed launcher and boots to its English title; a SIGSEGV run logs the backtrace;
the Windows filter's types match the SDK's (static_assert) and catch an access violation under Wine.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
